{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And unto the nobles of the children of Israel</b> — these are Nadab and Abihu and the elders mentioned (Exodus 24:1). He called them thus because the spirit of Elohim was drawn upon them, and likewise \"from its nobles I have called you\" (Isaiah 41:9) — the ones upon whom a spirit was drawn, or the great ones upon whom glory was drawn from the kingship." "And the reason for <b>He did not lay His hand</b> — because He said, \"and let not the priests and the people break through to ascend to HaShem, lest He break forth among them,\" He informed here that they were careful in this matter and He did not break forth among them, for the nobles of the children of Israel were worthy of what they beheld in this vision. And the reason is \"for they beheld Elohim,\" and they did not break through to ascend to HaShem." "And the reason for <b>and they ate and they drank</b> — that they ate there the shelamim offerings at the foot of the mountain before Elohim before they would return to their tents, for shelamim offerings require a partition and are eaten in Jerusalem within the wall (Zevaḥim 55a), and in Shiloh throughout the visible area (ibid. 112b), and here they were eaten before the altar at the foot of the mountain, not in the camp." "And the reason for <b>and they drank</b> — that they made rejoicing and a festival day, for it is an obligation to rejoice at the reception of the Torah, as He commanded regarding writing all the words of the Torah upon the stones: \"and you shall sacrifice shelamim offerings and you shall eat there and you shall rejoice before HaShem your Elohim\" (Deuteronomy 27:7). And it is written concerning Solomon (2 Chronicles 1:12): \"wisdom and knowledge are granted to you,\" etc., and immediately afterward: \"and he came to Jerusalem and made a feast for all his servants\" (1 Kings 3:15). And Rabbi Elazar said: From here that one makes a feast for the completion of the Torah (Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:9). And it is stated regarding David his father, when they contributed willingly to the building of the Temple: \"and they sacrificed to HaShem sacrifices and they offered burnt offerings to HaShem, etc., and they ate and they drank before HaShem on that day with great rejoicing\" (1 Chronicles 29:21–22), and likewise here, on the day of the wedding of the Torah, they did so."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:18:40.545907115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}